This is competent, thoughtful emotional intelligence work that shows strong self-reflection. However, it leans toward the analytical and strategic rather than the deeply relational. The debrief is actually more emotionally intelligent than the roleplay itself—it shows the respondent knows what was missing. The gap between the two suggests they understand EQ conceptually but may struggle to embody it in real-time, high-stakes moments.

